Log what each request actually asks to sample.

An OpenAI client that sends no sampling parameters gets the model's
`generation_config`, which here means `do_sample=true, temperature=1.0,
top_k=20, top_p=0.95`. That decides what speculation can do: greedy lookup
drafting does not apply, and probabilistic drafting beats point-mass fills. This
logs client address, prompt digest and the effective sampling parameters per
request (`VLLM_SAMPLING_LOG=1`), so the traffic is visible instead of inferred.

Log the sampling parameters of every incoming request, once, at INFO: the
source address identifies the client, the digest identifies the prompt
template, and temperature/top_p/top_k/min_p/tools/effort decide which speed
features apply (the history lookup serves greedy requests only). Read-only.

